<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">

  <!-- Meta tags (Part 1) -->
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <meta name="description" content="Practice with meta tags and CSS selectors">
  <meta name="author" content="Tanner Tinsley">

  <title>Meta Tags and CSS Selectors</title>

  <style>
    /* ELEMENT SELECTOR */
    body {
      font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 1rem;
      background-color: #f9f9f9;
    }

    /* CLASS SELECTOR */
    .highlight {
      color: #0056b3;
      font-weight: bold;
    }

    /* ID SELECTOR */
    #main-title {
      text-align: center;
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
    }

    /* DESCENDANT SELECTOR */
    section p {
      line-height: 1.6;
    }

    /* ATTRIBUTE SELECTOR */
    a[target="_blank"] {
      color: darkred;
    }

    /* PSEUDO-CLASS */
    a:hover {
      text-decoration: underline;
    }
  </style>
</head>

<body>

  <h1 id="main-title">Meta Tags & CSS Selectors</h1>

  <section>
    <p>
      This paragraph demonstrates <span class="highlight">CSS selectors</span>
      and how styles are applied using different selector types.
    </p>

    <p>
      Meta tags help control page behavior on different devices and improve
      accessibility and SEO.
    </p>
  </section>

  <p>
    Visit
    <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org" target="_blank">
      MDN Web Docs
    </a>
    to learn more.
  </p>

</body>
</html>
